  "question": {
    "text": "If the product of height and square of the radius of the greatest cone obtained by rotating a right-angled triangle of hypotenuse <math><mn>2</mn></math> meters about a side is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mi>k</mi><mrow><mn>3</mn><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt></mrow></mfrac></math>, then&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>k</mi></math>&nbsp;is equal to",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "16",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/nta_abhyas/jee_main/images/d1ed28d4-a3bd-486c-bf92-f5c5138e1d81.png\" style=\"max-width:100%; object-fit:contain\" style=\"width:1.96667in;height:1.37986in\" /></p><p>Let, the cone is obtained by rotating about&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>B</mi><mi>C</mi></math></p><p>From the diagram, the radius of the cone is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi><mi>B</mi></math>&nbsp;and the height is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>B</mi><mi>C</mi></math><br />The volume generated,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>V</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac><mi>&#960;</mi><msup><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>h</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac><mi>&#960;</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>-</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfenced><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mi>x</mi></mfenced></math><br />For maximum volume, <math><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><mi>V</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math><br /><math><mo>&#8658;</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn><msup><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow><mrow><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt></mrow></mfrac></math></p><p>&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8756;</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>&#960;</mi><mn>3</mn></mfrac><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mn>4</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac></mrow></mfenced><mfrac><mn>2</mn><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>16</mn><mi>&#960;</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>9</mn><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt></mrow></mfrac></math><br />Also,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>d</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>V</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac><mo>&#60;</mo><mn>0</mn></math></p><p>Hence,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mfenced><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>-</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>2</mn><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt></mfrac><mfenced><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mn>4</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>16</mn><mrow><mn>3</mn><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt></mrow></mfrac></math></p>",
    "image": null
  },
